# §9 properties — get/set accessors on interfaces and implementers (additive)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT ENTERS (additive; every existing member/field access parses and lowers byte-identically —
# docs/design/plano-secao9-properties.md §0-§7):
#   - THREE INERT `Function` FIELDS, in `src/parser/ast.tks`: `is_getter`/`is_setter`/`accessor_prop`,
#     false/false/"" in every constructor and passed through in every reconstruction. The `.tkb` codec
#     is UNCHANGED and reads them back false/"" (the `is_static` inert-field precedent).
#   - CONTEXTUAL `get`/`set` PARSING, in `src/parser/parse_decl.tks`. `get`/`set` stay ordinary
#     identifiers (never reserved — the corpus names hundreds of them); `accessor_kind_at` recognises
#     an accessor only when `get`/`set` in MEMBER position is followed by a NAME and `(`.
#     `parse_accessor`/`accessor_function` build a `Function` under the synthetic name with the flags
#     set; `parse_member_fn_or_accessor` routes the struct/class/trait/interface member loops.
#   - USE-SITE DESUGAR, in `src/checker/typer.tks`. `find_property`/`PropInfo` scan the receiver's
#     EFFECTIVE method surface for accessors (the flags, never the bare name, are the authority). A
#     READ (`type_field_access`) probes a property ONLY after field-absence (never on a visibility
#     failure): a getter desugars `a.prop` to `__get_prop()` via `type_method_call`; a get-less
#     property is a write-only error. A WRITE (`type_field_assign`) probes property-first: a setter
#     desugars `a.prop = v` to `__set_prop(v)` wrapped in a `TExprStmt`; a set-less property is a
#     read-only error; a compound `op=` on a property is a clean deferred error (plain `=` only).
#   - CONFORMANCE, in `src/checker/collect.tks`. An accessor requirement is an ordinary method
#     requirement (matched by the synthetic name); `requirement_desc` hides the synthetic name behind
#     property wording in the diagnostic (byte-identical text for every non-accessor requirement).
# WHAT DOES NOT ENTER: no auto-property (the backing field is explicit); struct implementers are
# get-only in this cut (a struct setter needs `mut self` machinery reported below); compound `op=` on
# a property is deferred to a follow-up; cross-library accessors (`.tkb` serialization) are a future
# additive extension. ZERO codegen/lowering `.tks` edited — an accessor is a method end to end.
#
# INERTNESS. Zero accessors exist in the corpus, so `find_property` returns null for every existing
# field access and both desugar sites run the historic path in the historic order (read probes only
# after field-absence; write probes first but null on every real field, the backing being `_prop`).
# `accessor_kind_at`/`parse_accessor` never fire (no `get`/`set` in member position followed by
# name+`(`), and `get`/`set` stay `Ident`, so every real `get`/`set` name parses unchanged. No existing
# field access newly routes through an accessor. The whole 153-file compiler re-checks and self-builds
# green.
#
